#ASSERT `s 661(3) the court may relieve the subscriber or director from his liability` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 661(3) the court may relieve the subscriber or director from his liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the function is named for a grant or a power and its "if" gate fails here, so it answers NOTHING and not JUST FALSE (fork F-grant-661-3)
#ASSERT `s 661(3) the court may relieve the subscriber or director from his liability` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 661(3) the court may relieve the subscriber or director from his liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the function is named for a grant or a power and its "if" gate fails here, so it answers NOTHING and not JUST FALSE (fork F-grant-661-3)
#ASSERT `s 661(3) the court may relieve the subscriber or director from his liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 661(4)(a) the subscriber or director may apply to the court for relief` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 661(4)(a) the subscriber or director may apply to the court for relief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the function is named for a grant or a power and its "if" gate fails here, so it answers NOTHING and not JUST FALSE (fork F-grant-661-4a)
#ASSERT `s 661(4)(a) the subscriber or director may apply to the court for relief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 661(4)(a) the subscriber or director may apply to the court for relief` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 661(4)(b) the court has the power to relieve him` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
