#ASSERT `s 661(4)(b) the court has the power to relieve him` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was `#ASSERT `s 661(4)(b) the court has the power to relieve him` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE`; the function is named for a grant or a power and its "if" gate fails here, so it answers NOTHING and not JUST FALSE (fork F-grant-661-4b)
#ASSERT `s 661(4)(b) the court has the power to relieve him` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
