-- ---- s 670 ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN pub IS A BOOLEAN, unpaid IS A BOOLEAN, payable IS A BOOLEAN, lender IS A BOOLEAN, credit IS A BOOLEAN, ordinary IS A BOOLEAN, rereg IS A BOOLEAN, existing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares`
`fixture: a charge` MEANS `s 670(1) lien or charge of a company on its own shares` WITH
    `s 670(1) the company is a public company` IS pub
    `s 670(2) the shares are not fully paid up` IS unpaid
    `s 670(2) the charge is for an amount payable in respect of the shares` IS payable
    `s 670(3)(a) the company's ordinary business includes the lending of money` IS lender
    `s 670(3)(b) the company's ordinary business consists of the provision of credit or the bailment of goods under a hire-purchase agreement, or both` IS credit
    `s 670(3) the charge arises in connection with a transaction entered into in the ordinary course of that business` IS ordinary
    `s 670(4) the company has been re-registered as a public company` IS rereg
    `s 670(4) the charge was in existence immediately before the application for re-registration` IS existing

-- arguments: public, unpaid, payable, lender, credit, ordinary course, re-registered, existing
